TarkovMapLite — third-party material and disclaimers
=====================================================

1. Map artwork
--------------
Map images are rasterised from the map SVGs in tools/maps-src/ or stitched
from the tarkov.dev tile images at https://assets.tarkov.dev/maps/.
Those SVGs come from the tarkov.dev map resources (https://github.com/the-hideout/tarkov-dev),
which in turn are traced from maps that belong to the game.

  * The PNGs here are derivatives (rendered at ~4000 px on the long edge,
    one image per floor with the ground layer hidden).
  * Reserve's Second_Floor through Fifth_Floor under Assets/maps/reserve/
    are tile-derived fallbacks, reprojected into the SVG base's coordinate frame.
    The ground and Bunkers images remain SVG-derived.
  * Assets/floor-extents.json preserves supported maps' building bounds and height
    rules from https://github.com/the-hideout/tarkov-dev/blob/main/src/data/maps.json
    (retrieved 2026-11-12). tools/sync-map-layers.py rebuilds these derivatives.
    Customs' fourth SVG floor and Shoreline/Interchange tile floors are likewise
    reprojected from the available artwork in their sibling variants.
  * They are provided for personal, non-commercial use together with this tool.
  * All rights to the original game artwork belong to Battlestate Games Limited.

If you are a rights holder and want a map removed, open an issue and it will be
deleted.

2. Game data
------------

Assets/story-tasks.json contains a factual story-objective catalogue derived from
szepiz/tarkov-quest-data/mapdata/story.json (2026-08-11 snapshot), which credits
tarkovtracker-org/tarkov-data-overlay for chapter structure and game objective
text. Chapter text is not claimed as CC0 or relicensed as this project's code.
https://github.com/szepiz/tarkov-quest-data/blob/16ca34ade3e4a874b83553ffc2f2e577be966fa9/mapdata/story.json
Hand-placed story coordinates are CC0-1.0 by szepiz, snapshot 2026-08-26:
https://github.com/szepiz/tarkov-quest-data/blob/main/api/firstparty/story-marks.json
https://github.com/szepiz/tarkov-quest-data/blob/main/LICENSE.md
Floor array order is factual map metadata from szepiz/tarkov-questing-companion,
mapdata.js, originating from tarkov.dev (the-hideout). No companion source code
or additional map artwork is shipped. tools/build-story-tasks.py reproduces the
join and converts floor indexes to layer IDs without executing JavaScript.

Task metadata in Assets/data-seed.json (471 matching task IDs) is supplemented
with factual trader, map, minimum-level, faction and Kappa/Lightkeeper fields
from the public tarkov.dev API snapshot dated 2026-09-14, preserved at:
https://github.com/sayser/TarkovTracker/blob/f4ad6a50be49bbba3c3791fd52aa042d99ce3cfd/tools/data/tarkov_tasks_raw.json
Only factual metadata is imported. The task text, item names and map geometry
remain from the sources below. Unmatched fields stay unknown. Reproduce the
metadata import with tools/build-task-metadata.py; pass the actual snapshot date
using --as-of and its pinned source URL using --source-url.

Assets/task-locations.json also imports factual objective IDs, map keys and x/y/z
positions from that same pinned snapshot. Reproduce with tools/build-task-locations.py.
Existing task text and area outlines are retained; positions fill missing locations.
One conflicting Oil Run point (-334.93, -101.46, -163.46) labelled Reserve is retained
in the exclusion list: the same snapshot contains its Customs counterpart at y=2.22,
matching the Customs objective text and the original polygon. Its snapshot-only
Reserve region tag is excluded as well. No invented replacement coordinate is used.

Assets/point-heights.json includes factual position heights from the public
tarkov.dev API snapshots distributed in sayser/TarkovTracker, Config/:
https://github.com/sayser/TarkovTracker/tree/f17c54542e78fb8ef3f3cd40081c84c321a69825/Config
(tarkov_extracts_raw.json, tarkov_switches_raw.json, tarkov_transits_raw.json,
tarkov_spawns_raw.json, tarkov_hazards_raw.json, tarkov_btr.json).
Loose-loot heights come from this project's existing Assets/markers.json.
Only factual coordinates are imported; no source code or map artwork is copied.
Explicit floor annotations and their sources are in Assets/point-floor-overrides.json.
Assets/data-seed.json is a snapshot of:

  * https://json.tarkov.dev/pve/tasks        (+ tasks_zh translations)
  * https://json.tarkov.dev/pve/items        (+ items_zh translations)
  * https://json.tarkov.dev/pve/maps         (+ maps_zh translations)

fetched on 2026-11-07. Task and item text, translations, loot spawn points,
extract and transit positions all originate from that API (project: tarkov.dev,
by the-hideout). Only the records referenced by task objectives are kept.

